{"title":"2013 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ann, Bill and Cathy went bowling. In bowling, each score is a whole number.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In his first two games, Bill’s scores were 108 and 125. His average score after three games was 115. What was his score in the third game?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since Bill's average after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30dbdabe000350d0a1272d1ec009a5d99e0c076d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$115$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, his total score for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183fc23bee93f31de8da4d7ecd27bad64310e8f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$115 \\times 3 = 345$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />. The total score for the first two games was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/2/05261207a6368617573dd8f7c36ca3396fc47659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108 + 125 = 233$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, for Bill's third game, his score was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/7/fa7c36673d3b5945d4a1b2771b03d2766f252ec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$345 - 233 = \\boxed{112}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232500\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 28/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 153/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1083/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.272      1 2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    6.272      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36970:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232500 and revision id 285866. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}